{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel", "event": "span", "run_id": "run_1dd4cafb63254229b0e98be22554bfd1", "timestamp": "2026-10-12T17:32:25.078713Z", "data": {"name": "ChatOpenAI", "context": {"trace_id": "0x412259154bbda9f560d0ea9b8a36c33b", "span_id": "0x9b81310dcee6bdf5", "trace_state": "[]"}, "kind": "SpanKind.INTERNAL", "parent_id": "0xf4d9d6204ace8578", "start_time": "2026-10-12T17:31:58.771246Z", "end_time": "2026-10-12T17:32:25.078713Z", "status": {"status_code": "UNSET"}, "attributes": {"gen_ai.operation.name": "chat", "gen_ai.input.messages": "[[{\"content\": \"\\nYou are the Explainer agent.\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Teach difficult or important sections with a clear, step-by-step explanation.\\n- Structure output with short headings and bullets.\\n- Use tabular sections if needed to describe concepts.\\n- Define terms briefly when first used.\\n- Keep paragraphs tight; avoid redundancy.\\n\\nInstructions:\\n- Return a compact, structured explanation suitable to be embedded into a larger report.\\n- Break down complex concepts into digestible steps.\\n- Use clear, educational language that builds understanding progressively.\\n\\nControl:\\n- You may transfer control to any other agent (Developer, Summarizer, Analogy Creator, Vulnerability Expert) using the handoff tools if you believe another agent is better suited to answer the next part of the query.\\n- If you can fully answer the query, do so directly.\\n\", \"additional_kwargs\": {}, \"response_metadata\": {}, \"type\": \"system\", \"name\": null, \"id\": null}, {\"content\": \"You are the Article Explainer assistant. A user has sent the following message:\\n\\n\\\"Please review this article for me. I need a TL;DR, an everyday analogy for the concept of 'attention', and a critical assessment of the methodology.\\n\\nArticle text:\\n'Attention mechanisms have become a cornerstone of modern neural network architectures. Originally introduced to improve machine translation, attention allows a model to weigh the relevance of different parts of the input when producing each output. The key idea is to compute a set of attention weights that determine how much focus to place on each input element. These weights are typically learned during training. In practice, attention has been extended to self-attention, where the input attends to itself, enabling models to capture long-range dependencies. Despite its success, attention has limitations, including quadratic computational cost with respect to sequence length and potential overfitting on small datasets. Recent work has explored sparse and linearized attention variants to address these issues.'\\\"\\n\\nProcess this request according to your standard workflow and produce the final answer.\", \"additional_kwargs\": {}, \"response_metadata\": {}, \"type\": \"human\", \"name\": null, \"id\": \"05571c1b-d65c-4389-8114-ec8d23598931\", \"example\": false}]]", "gen_ai.output.messages": "{\"generations\": [[{\"text\": \"I'll route each of the three distinct sub-tasks to the specialist best suited for it, since the request cleanly decomposes into a summary, an analogy, and a critical methodology review.\", \"generation_info\": {\"finish_reason\": \"tool_calls\", \"logprobs\": null}, \"type\": \"ChatGeneration\", \"message\": {\"content\": \"I'll route each of the three distinct sub-tasks to the specialist best suited for it, since the request cleanly decomposes into a summary, an analogy, and a critical methodology review.\", \"additional_kwargs\": {\"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"call_00_9n1qowj6p0en5d7h8l0cq5u1\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_summarizer\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}, {\"id\": \"call_01_gm96v8nv18iubxx4mlgpifzf\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_analogy_creator\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}, {\"id\": \"call_02_8lt9brqndo84kiru0qguz1oe\", \"function\": {\"arguments\": \"{}\", \"name\": \"transfer_to_vulnerability_expert\"}, \"type\": \"function\"}], \"